--- leg 1: inclusive forward cumsum ---
sl_fwd: every cell equals the host cumulative sum: true
sl_fwd: the scan survives optimize as exactly one Scan_loop: true
sl_fwd: the state node is neither an input nor an output of the linked routine: true
sl_fwd: the input and the trajectory are the routine's only input and output: true
sl_fwd: the state node stays virtual after optimize: true
optimized IR:

sl_fwd: scan i1 = 0 to 6 carrying [v2_sl_fwd_s <- v1_sl_fwd_s := 0.0] {
    v1_sl_fwd_s := (v2_sl_fwd_s + sl_fwd_x[i1]);
    sl_fwd_out[i1] := v1_sl_fwd_s;
  }
--- leg 2: backward cumsum (suffix sums) ---
sl_bwd: every cell equals the host cumulative sum: true
sl_bwd: the scan survives optimize as exactly one Scan_loop: true
sl_bwd: the state node is neither an input nor an output of the linked routine: true
sl_bwd: the input and the trajectory are the routine's only input and output: true
sl_bwd: the state node stays virtual after optimize: true
--- leg 3: online softmax (running max, rescaled normalizer) ---
every running normalizer is within 1e-5 relative of the host recurrence: true
the final normalizer equals the direct sum of exp(x - max x) within 1e-5 relative: true
the trajectory is strictly increasing, as a sum of positive terms rescaled to a growing max: true
both carried scalars are counted, and no other scan is in the routine: true
--- leg 4: per-row scan under an outer loop, Serial vs Grid ---
serial outer loop: every cell equals the host per-row prefix sum: true
Grid-annotated outer loop: every cell agrees with the serial twin: true
--- leg 5: an undeclared scan output materializes (Non_virtual 148) ---
the scan output was refused as a virtualization candidate with provenance 148: true
the scan output is decided non-virtual, so the consumer reads its buffer: true
the consumer's read of the trajectory survives as a buffer read, not an inlined scope: true
the consumer computes twice the prefix sums: true
--- leg 5b: a candidate whose computation contains a scan materializes (148) ---
the candidate computed through a scan was refused with provenance 148: true
the scan survives as the candidate's materialized producer: true
the consumer reads each row's total from the buffer: true
--- leg 6: malformed scans are refused by name, at both pipeline gates ---
a next written only under a guard is refused: true
a next never written is refused: true
a next written twice is refused: true
a prev written in the body is refused: true
a materialized state node is refused: true
an init reading carried state is refused: true
a next read by a statement before the one that writes it is refused: true
a next read by its own defining statement is refused: true
an id shared by two carried pairs is refused: true
an init mentioning the scan index is refused: true
a state node left undeclared (neither virtual nor materialized) is refused: true
a Declare_local of a carried id inside the body is refused: true
a Local_scope binder reusing a carried id inside the body is refused: true
a tensor-buffer access to the state node elsewhere in the routine is refused: true
a read of a carried local after the scan is refused: true
a next read early through a Tile_mma fallback is refused: true
a tensor-buffer access to the state node inside a Tile_mma fallback is refused: true
a Staged_compilation inside the scan body is refused: true
a carried pair over two different nodes is refused: true
the backend refuses a malformed scan handed through the prelowered seam: true
--- leg 6a: a dead range is a no-op, inits included ---
the dead scan is dropped by optimize: true
a node read only by a dead scan's init is not a routine input: true
the trajectory node keeps its seeded sentinel in every cell: true
--- leg 6b: a half-precision state rounds the running sum every step ---
a single-precision state accumulates all six increments (2054): true
a half-precision state rounds each step back to 2048, so the sum stays at 2048: true
--- leg 7: schedule ops decline the scan's index and the loops inside it ---
Retype of the scan's own index declines for want of a For_loop: true
Split of the scan's own index declines for want of a For_loop: true
Unroll of a loop nested inside the scan body declines: the scan is opaque to locate and rewrite: true
the harness traversal reaches the loop inside the scan body exactly once: true
the nested loop computes prefix sum times (1 + k) in every cell: true
--- leg 8: the canonical rendering sees the recurrence and only the recurrence ---
a fresh lowering of the same scan renders identically (alpha-renamed symbols and ids): true
Forward and Backward render differently: true
swapping a carried pair's prev and next renders differently: true
rendering: carry <sl_dg_s>.0<-<sl_dg_s>.1:=0.;scan b0=0..6@Forward{setl <sl_dg_s>.1:=Add(getl(<sl_dg_s>.0)@Single_prec,get <sl_dg_x>[b0,]@Single_prec);set <sl_dg_out>[b0,]:=getl(<sl_dg_s>.1);}
